The function is already a single branch plus one indexed load; I hoisted `profile` into a local pointer so the null check and the dereference use one load, letting the compiler emit a tighter branch-and-load sequence.

```cpp
FIT_UINT16 Field::GetNumSubFields(void) const
{
    const Profile* p = profile;
    if ((p == NULL) || (profileIndex >= p->numFields))
        return 0;
    return p->fields[profileIndex].numSubFields;
}
```